# DURABLE REPRO — the THIRD `__gorget_closure_call_N` construction site
# (non-identifier callee arm at `src/ir/lowering/exprs/calls.rs` — grep-verify
# the current site with `grep -n 'lower_expr(ctx, builder, &arg.node.value)' \
# src/ir/lowering/exprs/calls.rs` — as of Track B1 tip the arm is at
# `:2196`) still lowers args via naive `lower_expr(&arg.node.value)`, so an
# indirect call whose callee is a non-identifier expression (`arr[0](x)`,
# `make_adder(3)(x)`, `shared.get()()`) SEGFAULTS on both C and LLVM even after
# Track B1 closes the two identifier-callee arms.
#
# ROOT: `callee_local` in this arm is a temp materialised from `lower_expr`, so
# it has no `callable_return_type` / `callable_param_types` /
# `callable_param_ownerships` sidecar (the four function-registration paths in
# `src/ir/lowering/functions.rs` + the fifth in `src/ir/lowering/stmts/mod.rs`
# only fire on identifier bindings). AND `GirType::FnPtr { params, return_type }`
# at `src/ir/types.rs:72-75` carries plain param `TypeId`s with no
# `param_ownerships` axis: the writer at `src/ir/lowering/types.rs:590-596` drops
# the `Type::Function`'s param-ownership sigils. So a sidecar transplant on this
# arm is not enough — the FnPtr GIR type itself has already forgotten the `&`.
#
# REFERENCE-GRADE FIX: extend `GirType::FnPtr` with
# `param_ownerships: Vec<Ownership>`, write at every FnPtr construction site
# (`src/ir/lowering/types.rs` `Type::Function` arm + any other FnPtr writer),
# then consult the FnPtr's param types AND ownerships at
# `src/ir/lowering/exprs/calls.rs`'s non-identifier arm to route each arg
# through `lower_call_arg`. Out of Track B1's scope because it touches every
# `FnPtr` writing site.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): 101. Same reference-grade semantics as the
# graduated `callable_amp_fntype_writethrough.gg` sibling — the closure body's
# write-through must land on the caller's `a`.
#
# AXIS / CELL: the non-identifier-callee cell of the callable-indirection axis.
# Sibling of `callable_amp_fntype_writethrough.gg` (identifier callee, LOCAL)
# and `sound_callable_amp_param_projection.gg` (identifier callee, PARAM); the
# discriminator is the callee shape (Vector index vs. bare name), not the arg's
# root.
#
# MEASURED 2026-07-27 at Track B1 tip: `gg check` clean, `gg build` clean, binary
# exit 139 on both C and LLVM. Un-ignore when the `FnPtr param_ownerships`
# extension lands.
void bump(int &n):
    n = n + 100

void main():
    int a = 1
    Vector[Callable[void(int &)]] arr = []
    arr.push(bump)
    arr[0](&a)
    print(a)
